    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, which is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:108`). I've marked each step as a **validation** (can reject the request) or a **side-effect** (mutates the owner, DB, or logs).\n\n## 1. Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Validation \u2014 authorization** (`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`, line 108): caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else `403`.\n2. **Validation \u2014 request-body bean validation** (`@Valid @RequestBody` in the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner`, `OwnersApi.java:86`) on the `OwnerFieldsDto` fields; any failure \u2192 `400`:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*`, `@Size(1,255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - `postcode`: `@Size(min 4, max 4)` (optional)\n\n## 2. Mapping\n\n3. **Side-effect \u2014 map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (line 112, `OwnerMapperImpl.toOwner`): copies firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone, email, postcode, registrationDate, birthDate. Note `sharesHousehold` is **not** mapped onto the entity \u2014 it is read separately from the DTO later.\n\n## 3. `normalizeNewOwner(owner)` \u2014 field normalization + rejections (lines 249\u2013277)\n\nRuns in this exact order:\n\n4. **Side-effect / Validation \u2014 address**: `Owner.normalizeAddress` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand whole-word `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). If empty after normalization \u2192 `400`; otherwise the normalized address is stored.\n5. **Validation / Side-effect \u2014 telephone**: `Telephones.toE164` (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep `+`/country code, else assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`; require 8\u201315 digits; enforce national-number length: `+61`\u21929 digits, `+1`\u219210). `null` result \u2192 `400`; otherwise the E.164 value is stored.\n6. **Side-effect / Validation \u2014 email** (only if non-null): lower-cased and stored, then checked against the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Blocked domain \u2192 `400`.\n7. **Validation \u2014 postcode/locality**: `owner.postcodeValidForLocality()` (absent postcode OK; otherwise must be 4 digits and, if the locality has a known range NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099, fall within it). `false` \u2192 `400`.\n8. **Side-effect / Validation \u2014 registrationDate**: if null, default to today (`LocalDate.now()`); if a supplied date is after today \u2192 `400`.\n9. **Side-effect \u2014 roll to business day**: `rollToBusinessDay` advances Saturday\u2192Monday, Sunday\u2192Monday; the result is stored as the registration date.\n\n## 4. Population/quota checks (against all existing owners)\n\n10. **Validation \u2014 daily limit** (line 116): if \u2265 100 existing owners already carry this registration date \u2192 `429 Too Many Requests`.\n11. **Validation \u2014 city capacity** (line 119): if \u2265 50 existing owners (case-insensitive city match) already in this city \u2192 `409 Conflict`.\n\n## 5. Household resolution\n\n12. **Side-effect \u2014 householdId** (line 122): `owner.setHouseholdId(owner.computeHouseholdId())` (deterministic hash of normalized last name + postcode).\n13. **Validation \u2014 household conflict** (lines 123\u2013127): reads `sharesHousehold` from the DTO; finds any existing owner in the same household (same last name + postcode). If a member exists **and** `sharesHousehold` is not `true` \u2192 `409 Conflict`.\n\n## 6. `assignDerivedAttributes(owner, declaredHouseholdMember)` \u2014 persisted derived fields (lines 358\u2013365)\n\nAll are side-effects on the owner, in this order (order matters \u2014 customer code feeds the membership number):\n\n14. **Side-effect \u2014 customerCode**: `computeCustomerCode()` (`<REGION>-<HASH8>`).\n15. **Side-effect \u2014 namesakeCount**: count of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n16. **Side-effect \u2014 membershipNumber**: `<customerCode>-M<YY>` from the registration year.\n17. **Side-effect \u2014 bulkSignupWarning**: `true` if > 80 existing owners share the registration date.\n18. **Side-effect \u2014 householdSize**: count of existing owners with the same `householdId`, plus 1.\n19. **Side-effect \u2014 possibleDuplicate / possibleDuplicateOf**: if a declared household member, both cleared (`false`/`null`); otherwise flagged `true` with the lowest-id existing owner that shares last name + postcode but has a **different** telephone.\n\n## 7. Persist + finish\n\n20. **Side-effect \u2014 persist** (line 130): `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (transactional), which assigns the id.\n21. **Side-effect \u2014 audit log** (line 131): `AUDIT.info(...)` logging id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n22. **Side-effect \u2014 response**: map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return `201 Created`.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the quota/household/derivation checks (steps 10\u201319) all re-scan `findAllOwners()` in memory rather than querying, and none of steps 10\u201322 run in a single transaction (only `saveOwner` itself is `@Transactional`), so the count-based checks are evaluated against pre-save state without concurrency protection."
